"""Layered memory: L1 events are the only authority; L2–L4 are rebuilt from them.

* L1 — append-only ``duckmind.provenance.Event`` records, chained by SHA-256.
* L2 — episodes (visits, touch bursts, play sessions) segmented from L1.
* L3 — distilled facts ("what the duck remembers"), each with evidence event IDs,
  a deterministic strength (spacing makes it stronger, time without support fades
  it) and bi-temporal fields.
* L4 — a templated diary; every sentence cites the events behind it.

Forgetting a memory appends a ``memory.forget`` tombstone. Rebuilding with the
tombstoned events excluded is exactly "as if it never happened" for L2–L4.
"""

